    {
      "id": "land-regular-45-01",
      "status": "revised-candidate-pending-lead",
      "characterId": "beatrice-bark",
      "characterName": "Beatrice Bark",
      "platform": "facebook",
      "format": "regular",
      "title": "Still on the stem",
      "prose": "I was going to make this cherry last.\n\nThe others had gone down almost before I tasted them. This one I touched with my tongue, still hanging from its stem. Turned my head farther around the trunk. Held it between my lips. Warm skin, then a little split, and the juice came out.\n\nI wanted more of that. Pulled.\n\nSwallowed it.\n\nKept my mouth open against the empty stem for a moment. Licked it. There was still a little sweetness there, so I licked it again, hugging the tree with all four feet.",
      "mediaIndex": 9,
      "alt": "A black bear clings around a leafy tree trunk, head tilted sideways, with its tongue extended beneath a dark cherry.",
      "visibleScene": "Black bear gripping trunk, tilted head, tongue and individual fruit at mouth; foliage and branches. NPS expressly identifies eating a single cherry.",
      "fictionBoundary": "Intent to prolong the taste, prior cherries, skin splitting, pulling, swallowing and licking the emptied stem are fictional sequence around visible tongue-to-cherry contact. No companion, descent or documented before/after claimed.",
      "ageSex": "Independent adult-sized female in fiction; source does not record sex or exact age. No pregnancy or motherhood claim.",
